48
00:03:58,039 --> 00:04:04,039
Everywhere's rigging merges the outfit with the avatar's joints, allowing them to move together.

49
00:04:04,039 --> 00:04:13,039
This rigging process also involves weight painting, which determines how much each part of the outfit is influenced by the movement of the avatar's joints.

50
00:04:13,039 --> 00:04:20,039
This rigging process involves setting up and creating the controllable structure for the movement of the avatar and the outfit.

51
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:29,040
Clo and Marvelous Designer excel in creating highly detailed and realistic clothing animations through specialized garment simulations.

52
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:38,040
However, due to the large data sizes resulting from simulation-based clothing animations, they are impractical for use in games.

53
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:48,040
In the gaming industry, a different optimization approach, known as rigging, is utilized to synchronize the movement of the outfit and avatar.

54
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,040
Everywhere's rigging is designed to synchronize the movement of the outfit and avatar.

55
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:54,040
Everywhere's rigging is designed to synchronize the movement of the outfit and avatar for optimal performance.

56
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:59,040
Everywhere's rigging puts the clothing based on the rigging information of the avatar.

57
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:08,040
The avatar should have joints in a human-like form, and rigging only works when the avatar is in an A or T pose.

58
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:17,040
